  "notes": {
    "sanitize-type-blindness": {
      "id": "sanitize-type-blindness",
      "category": "issue",
      "status": "open",
      "title": "applyPolicy is type-blind and cannot mask non-string fields",
      "body": "applyPolicy/hashValue stringify every value (fmt.Sprintf %v), so a policy\nmatch on a non-string slot (array/object/number) produces a string. The\ncontainer pipeline (core/document/sanitize.go sanitizeContainerLeaves)\ncorrectly refuses to write a masked string into a non-string slot and\nreturns \"cannot store sanitized value ... in \u003ctype\u003e slot\", which fails\nSanitize() for the WHOLE document. Real-world fallout: hestia's global\n(?i)auth pattern matched the array field `authors` of its dynamic `notes`\ncollection, so every document failed sanitization and the query API\nsilently returned data:[] with correct pagination counts (the HTTP layer\ndrops documents whose Sanitize errors).\n\nDecision (2026-08-22): fix belongs at the app config level for now (keep\nmasking rules targeted/collection-scoped so patterns only ever hit string\nfields); no library change shipped. If this is ever fixed here, likely\nshapes are: element-wise masking for arrays of strings, skipping\nnon-maskable slots with a warning, or schema-type-aware policies threaded\nthrough FieldMaskConfig.\n",
      "location": {
        "file": "core/sanitize/sanitizer.go",
        "startLine": 116,
        "startCol": 3,
        "endLine": 134,
        "endCol": 3
      },
      "hash": "d4520fa8abf5db8f"
    }
  },
